# Engineering workflow

Inspect the current code and user constraints, implement authorized work, and verify the affected contract. Ask for missing information only when it blocks a necessary step.

Use local tests and direct source inspection. Separate code verification from live model-quality and operating-cost claims. Report meaningful checks and material limitations.

Preserve user changes. Keep private sources, credentials, trial notes and generated libraries out of commits. Trial preparation does not authorize model calls, data publication or client configuration changes.
